This regex will match and remove any date in the format of DD-MM-YYYY or DD/MM/YYYY. The `\b` is a word boundary, `\d{1,2}` matches 1 or 2 digits, `[-/]` matches either a hyphen or a forward slash, and `\d{4}` matches exactly 4 digits.

You can also use this regex to match dates in the format of DD MMM YYYY or DD MMMM YYYY
