This regex will match and remove any date in the format of DD MMM YYYY or DD MMMM YYYY. The `\b` is a word boundary, `\d{1,2}` matches 1 or 2 digits, `[A-Za-z]{3,9}` matches 3 to 9 letters (which represents the month), and `\d{4}` matches exactly 4 digits.

You can also use this regex to match dates in the format of DD MMM YYYY or DD MMMM YYYY with optional year
```
