    field: 'date',
    type: 'date',
    valueGetter: params => {
      return moment(params.value).format('YYYY-MM-DD');
    }
  }
];
```
This will format the date value in the `date` column to the format `YYYY-MM-DD`.

If you really need to use `valueSetter`, you can use it to set the value of the cell, but you'll need to return the formatted value. Here is an example:
```
const columnDefs = [
  {
    field: 'date',
    type: 'date',
    valueSetter: params => {
      return moment(params.value).format('YYYY-MM-DD');
    }
  }
];
```
